---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
const tour = [
  ['/', 'Homepage', 'Shared navigation, branding and footer'],
  ['/use-cases/', 'Use Cases', '74 stories with search, sorting and grouped views'],
  ['/openstack-for-ai/', 'OpenStack for AI', 'Editorial content, media and quote carousel'],
  ['/vmware-migration-to-openstack/', 'VMware migration', 'Marketing page and research guide'],
  ['/community/', 'Community', 'Contribution choices and project resources'],
  [
    '/software/project-navigator/openstack-components/',
    'Software catalogue',
    'Existing React application inside Astro',
  ],
  [
    '/summit/boston-2017/',
    'Boston Summit archive',
    'Structured historical highlights, sponsors, FAQs and venues',
  ],
  ['/use-cases/science/', 'Science and HPC', 'Structured industry content and research'],
  [
    '/community/supporting-organizations/',
    'Supporting organizations',
    'Organizations and public profiles',
  ],
  ['/coa/', 'Certification', 'Exam information and training partners'],
];
---

<Layout title="OpenStack Astro — demo guide and readiness | OpenStack">
  <main id="main" class="status">
    <p class="eyebrow">Foundation review</p>
    <h1>OpenStack.org, built with Astro</h1>
    <p>
      The proposed website keeps content in Git, uses HTML-forward Astro templates, and integrates
      the existing React software application within one shared header and footer. This protected
      review site is independent of production and has no SilverStripe page proxy.
    </p>
    <h2>Suggested demo tour</h2>
    <div class="tour">
      {tour.map(([url, title, description]) => (
        <a href={url}>
          <h3>{title}</h3>
          <p>{description}</p>
          <span>Explore →</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <h2>What is working</h2>
    <p>
      The 208 imported editorial records now have native renderers, including specialized summit and
      industry templates. Community, learning, certification, company profiles, research readers,
      search, and the software catalogue have their own native routes. Research PDFs and approved
      images are served from private Cloudflare R2.
    </p>
    <h2 id="authentication">What remains before production</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Application sign-in:</strong> reviewer access works through Cloudflare Access.
        OpenStackID login and shared application sessions still need Astro-specific configuration
        and verification.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Content editing:</strong> editorial content is versioned in this repository. The
        Git-based CMS selection and publishing integration remain open; there is no connected editor
        login here yet.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Software:</strong> the React catalogue works with the migrated development snapshot.
        Production service data, identity, permissions and refresh must be verified.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Marketplace and Videos:</strong> their pages explain the agreed direction, findings
        and outstanding integration decisions.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Additional routes:</strong> schedules, legacy account workflows and content outside
        the imported set still show explicit review notices. Native rendering counts do not certify
        full production parity.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Launch audit:</strong> complete SEO, Open Graph, redirects, accessibility,
        analytics/consent, editorial workflow and operational checks. This site remains protected
        and noindex.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <a href="/marketplace/">Marketplace status</a> · <a href="/videos/">Video library status</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="https://beta.openstack.org/">SvelteKit comparison ↗</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
<style>
  .status {
    max-width: 1120px;
    margin: 48px auto;
    padding: 0 24px 64px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #294d68;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  .tour {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .tour > a {
    padding: 20px 24px;
    border: 1px solid #d6e1e8;
    border-radius: 6px;
    text-decoration: none;
    background: #f6f9fb;
  }
  .tour > a:hover,
  .tour > a:focus-visible {
    border-color: #ed1944;
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .tour p {
    color: #486375;
    margin: 8px 0;
  }
  .tour span {
    color: #006b94;
  }
  li {
    margin: 14px 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .tour {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
